From 907fade94b5e9070221c4df355d680cc84774a82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:37:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 39/41] [TSReader] Keep the segment of a PES header across a
 segment end, and give each stream a hold clock

Round 12 findings (Sol), both from a7866dd:

- A segment that ended inside the header of the next PES lost the PTS
  diff: the PES start waits for the rest of the header before the PES
  has an entry in the buffer, and the next segment dropped that
  segment. AddPesSegments now also keeps the segment of a PES whose
  header is not complete.
- The 1 s limit of held audio took one first DTS for all other streams.
  A subtitle PTS 0.5 s after the video set that DTS, and the audio
  waited 1.5 s of video. Each other stream now has a first DTS of its
  own, and the first stream with more than 1 s releases the audio.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
